```
Need `setLang`? loadSettings calls setLang. Good.

Class:

```
class AetheriaApp {
 constructor() {
  this.settings=loadSettings();
  this.screenEl=document.getElementById('screen');
  this.overlay=document.getElementById('overlay');
  this.audio=new AudioEngine(this.settings);
  this.tradeClient=new TradeClient();
  this.game=null; this.engine=null; this.hud=null; this.panels=null; this.menuCleanup=null; this.installPrompt=null;
  App.settings=this.settings; App.screen=this;
  document.body.classList.toggle('reduce-motion', Boolean(this.settings.reduceMotion));
  this.bindInstall();
  this.bindGlobal();
  this.registerServiceWorker();
 }
```
But `this.screenEl` might be null if script loaded before DOM? Script at end body, so fine. Could use getElementById in methods if needed.

`bindGlobal`:
```
const unlock = () => { this.audio.unlock(); ... };
document.addEventListener('pointerdown', unlock, {once:false}); remove after? use once? `{ once:true }` on both pointerdown/keydown means if first pointerdown, keydown listener still there but audio.started true; harmless. Use once.
window.addEventListener('beforeunload', ()=>{ if(this.game) saveNow(true); });
document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', ()=>{ if(document.hidden && this.game) saveNow(true); });
window.addEventListener('beforeinstallprompt', e=>{ e.preventDefault(); const prompt=e; this.installPrompt=async()=>{ prompt.prompt(); await prompt.userChoice.catch(()=>{}); this.installPrompt=null; };});
window.addEventListener('appinstalled', ()=>{ this.installPrompt=null; showToast(t('menu.installDone')??'...')}); // no key. skip.
```
Need no missing key. Don't toast.

`bindInstall` integrated.

`start()`:
```
start() {
 this.goMenu();
 const boot=document.getElementById('boot');
 setTimeout(()=>{ boot?.classList.add('leaving'); setTimeout(()=>boot?.remove(),800); }, 500);
}
```
Before goMenu, maybe ensure app has proper font. okay.

`goMenu()`:
```
if(this.game){ saveNow(true); }
this.refreshMenu();
```
`refreshMenu()`:
```
this.destroyWorld();
this.game=null; App.game=null; App.engine=null; App.ui=null;
window.__AETHERIA_PLAYER__=null; window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__=null;
this.menuCleanup?.(); this.menuCleanup=null;
this.screenEl.innerHTML=''; this.overlay.innerHTML='';
this.tradeClient.disconnect();
this.menuCleanup=renderMenu(this);
```
Wait if refreshMenu called from menu settings, `this.game` already null. `destroyWorld` sets screenEl.innerHTML empty; then render. Fine.
`goMenu` from in-game: `saveNow(true)`, then refresh. `refreshMenu` nulls game after save. Good.
`resetToMenu()`:
```
deleteGame();
this.refreshMenu();
showToast(t('common.deleted'),'good');
```
But `showToast` after menu render; toast layer. Good.
`gotoCreate()`:
```
this.destroyWorld(); this.game=null; App.game=null; ...
this.menuCleanup?.();...
this.screenEl.innerHTML=''; overlay...
this.menuCleanup=renderCreate(this);
```
`renderCreate` returns cleanup. Good.
`startGame(player, saved=null)`:
```
this.destroyWorld();
if(!player) return;
recalc(player);
if(!Number.isFinite(player.hp)||player.hp<=0) player.hp=player.stats.maxHp;
if(saved) { this.game={...saved, player, settings:this.settings}; }
else { this.game=createGame(player); }
this.game.settings=this.settings;
App.settings=this.settings; App.game=this.game; App.screen=this;
this.tradeClient.disconnect();
this.panels=new Panels(this);
this.hud=new WorldHud(this);
this.menuCleanup?.(); this.menuCleanup=null;
this.screenEl.innerHTML=''; this.overlay.innerHTML=''; closeModal();
this.hud.attach();
saveNow(true);
this.audio.unlock();
```
Order: `WorldHud.attach` creates engine and sets screen.engine, attaches. Need `panels` before attach (HUD uses). Good.
`this.screen.engine` from previous? destroyWorld sets null.
`continueGame()`:
```
const saved=loadGame();
if(!saved?.player){ this.gotoCreate(); return; }
const p=saved.player;
if(!p.equipment) p.equipment={};
if(!p.inventory) p.inventory=[];
if(!p.storage) p.storage=[];
if(!p.stones) p.stones=[];
if(!p.visited) p.visited={};
if(!p.discoveredZones) p.discoveredZones=[p.zoneId||'greendale'];
recalc(p);
if(!p.hp || p.hp<=0) p.hp=p.stats.maxHp;
this.startGame(p,{saved});
```
`recalc` uses `player.stones.find`; ensure stones array before recalc. Also `p.quests` etc maybe. Add defaults.
`startGame` calls recalc again; fine.
`saved` may be `{version,savedAt,createdAt,settings,player}`. game.settings set. Good.

`destroyWorld()`:
```
this.panels?.dispose?.(); this.panels=null;
this.hud?.destroy?.(); this.hud=null;
this.engine=null; App.engine=null;
```
But `hud.destroy` calls engine.detach; engine remains local in hud. set screen.engine=null. Also `this.engine` never set separately? In `startGame`, world.js sets screen.engine; main `this.engine` remains null. Engine.js `getHudState` no. We use `this.engine` in travel. Should set `this.engine = this.screen.engine` after `hud.attach`. In `startGame` after attach: `this.engine = this.screen.engine`.
`destroyWorld`: `this.engine=null; this.screen.engine=null;`.
`this.screenEl.innerHTML=''`; overlay.

But `panels.dispose` calls `screen.engine.setPaused(false)` before engine detach. harmless.

`travel(zoneId)` as above. Use `this.engine || this.screen.engine`.

`applyLanguage()`:
```
this.audio.setSettings(this.settings);
if(this.game && this.engine){ const p=this.game.player; this.startGame(p,{saved:this.game}); }
else this.refreshMenu();
```
But `startGame` disconnects trade and recreates; okay. `saved:this.game` includes game.player same p. `startGame` spreads; ensures settings. It will `saveNow(true)` and engine loadZone restore. Good.
However `startGame` calls `recalc`, if hp persisted. fine.
Maybe preserve `this.game` createdAt. yes.

`tick(dt)`: `this.hud?.tick(dt)`.
`tutorialStep(step)`: `this.hud?.tutorialStep(step)`.
`onDeath()`: `this.hud?.onDeath()`.
`openPanel(name)`: `this.panels?.open(name)`.
`openDialogue(npc)`: `this.panels?.openDialogue(npc)`.
`toggleMenu`.
`toast(text,type)`: `showToast(text,type)`.

`registerServiceWorker()`:
```
if (!('serviceWorker' in navigator)) return;
if (location.protocol==='file:') return;
window.addEventListener('load',()=>{ navigator.serviceWorker.register('./sw.js').catch(()=>{});});
```
But start called at module eval after DOM loaded; `window.load` may have already fired? Module scripts execute before load; add listener still works. Or directly register. Use `navigator.serviceWorker.register('./sw.js').catch(...)`.

`bindInstall`:
```
window.addEventListener('beforeinstallprompt',(event)=>{ event.preventDefault(); const prompt=event; this.installPrompt=async()=>{ prompt.prompt(); try{await prompt.userChoice;}catch{} this.installPrompt=null;};});
```
Note `menu.js` checks `if (!screen.installPrompt) return '';` and `screen.installPrompt?.()`; good.

`screen.installPrompt` default undefined.

`applyLanguage` also `document.body.classList.toggle('reduce-motion')`.

Need `saveSettings` import used? In applyLanguage? not. In language menu handled. But maybe not. Remove if unused. We do use in constructor? no. But maybe `applyLanguage` should `saveSettings(this.settings)`. Do.

`toast` common uses `showToast` alias.

`window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__` set in world attach. Also menu? common language switch inside menu saves `window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__ ?? {}` but menu `langSwitch` calls `screen.refreshMenu`; `bindLanguage` in menu passes onChange; it calls saveSettings on empty settings object if __AETHERIA_SETTINGS__ not set. Hmm, in menu, `window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__` is only set in world. So language switch in main menu uses `{}` and overwrites settings to `{}` in localStorage! That's a bug: `common.bindLanguage` calls `saveSettings(window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__ ?? {})`. If we set `window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__ = this.settings` in main constructor, then menu language switch saves actual settings. Do that. Also update on apply? settings object reference persists. Good.

`settings.lang` needs update when setLang called. `bindLanguage` calls setLang(id) but doesn't update settings.lang before save. In menu, `saveSettings(window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__)` saves stale `lang` (old). Then `refreshMenu` renders `langSwitch` based on `getLang` (updated in memory), but localStorage has old lang. On reload, loadSettings sets old lang. That's a bug. Need fix common.bindLanguage to set settings.lang. Could edit:
```
const settings = window.__AETHERIA_SETTINGS__;
if(settings) { settings.lang=id; saveSettings(settings); }
```
Also menu's settings object is `screen.settings`; `openSettings` bindSettings: after setLang, `saveSettings(settings)` but settings.lang stale too. Need set. Better edit `bindLanguage`:
